  abstract = {Presents a historical survey of the origin and development of psychoanalysis. Points out that Breuer was unable to give a complete theory and a sufficient explanation of hysteria. Further investigations and dealing with patients led to the concepts of repression, sublimation, hypnosis, transfer and interpretation of dreams. Views that psychoanalytic investigations trace the history of symptoms of a disease and show that the pathogenic wishes are related to erotic impulses. It has been concluded that the disturbances in the erotic sphere are the chief etiological factors for most mental diseases. The discovery of the phenomena of transfer and infantile sexuality was important in understanding the functioning of human mind. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)},
