  abstract = {Describes mathematical and statistical models for factor invariance (INV), demonstrating that factor INV is a condition of measurement INV. In any study of change (as over age) measurement INV is necessary for valid inference and interpretation. Two important forms of factor INV are distinguished: configural and metric. Tests for factor INV and the range of tests from strong to weak are illustrated with multiple group factor and structural equation modeling analyses. The tests are for models of the organization and age changes of intellectual abilities. The models are derived from current theory of fluid (Gf) and crystallized (Gc) abilities. The models are made manifest with measurements of the Wechsler Adult Intelligence Scale—Revised (WAIS—R) in the standardization sample (N\enspace =\enspace 1,880). Conceptual principles of multivariate methods of data analysis are presented in terms of substantive issues of importance for the psychology of aging. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)},
